WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.090
As one of the Teen Titans' most memorable
enemies, Trigon has shown up to menace nearly

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:09.980
every incarnation of the team, but what is
it that makes this demon so memorable?

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:15.080
Join us as we dive into the forbidden history
of Raven's fearsome father and all the havoc

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:15.960
he has wreaked.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.060
Trigon, unstoppable avatar of evil and bringer
of doom, began his immortal life as a mistake

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.620
on the part of the good guys.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:28.640
Centuries ago, a band of humans who were weary
of human suffering created a haven between

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.080
dimensions, the place that would become Azarath.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.780
It was paradise built by human hands.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:39.620
Led by Azar, a visionary mystic, the pacifists
of Azarath decided to cement their utopia

00:00:39.629 --> 00:00:41.239
by purging it of all evil.

00:00:41.239 --> 00:00:45.500
At first, they seemed to have succeeded in
this monumental task, but the dark energy

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.700
began to coalesce into something altogether
darker.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:53.280
Ages passed, until a sect on a doomed and
distant planet summoned a dark spirit in a

00:00:53.289 --> 00:00:55.100
last-ditch attempt at survival.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:00.200
The cast-off energy inhabited a woman of the
order, and nine months later, Trigon was born.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.480
His first act was to slaughter his mother
and her compatriots, which was the beginning

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.720
of a long and bloody career of conquest.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.760
Like many comic characters, Trigon doesn't
have one singular origin.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:17.000
The "New 52," a line-wide reboot of the DC
universe's characters and continuity, gave

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.150
Trigon an alternate origin rooted in even
more potent forms of evil.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:26.340
According to Teen Titans #23.1, a "Villain
Month" special where the bad guys stepped

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:30.940
into the spotlight, Trigon was created through
the folly of a trio of alien beings known

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.000
as the Divine.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.360
Acting as interstellar peacekeepers, they
discovered a world they'd thought was cleansed

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.180
of wickedness had devolved into brutal chaos.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.980
After finding the man responsible, the Divine
attempted to quarantine him by feeding him

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:48.280
to the Heart of Darkness, an inescapable abyss
to which they consigned all evil.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.460
But the culprit was a juvenile Trigon, and
his power was too great.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:57.120
Instead of being consumed by the Heart, he
consumed it, thus devouring the millions of

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.540
wicked souls the Divine had placed within
it.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:04.720
Flooded with power, Trigon killed the Divine
and resolved to blanket the universe in his evil.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:08.620
But he quickly found that he couldn't escape
a barrier the Divine had erected.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:14.100
Undaunted, he began to transport female humanoids
his way, to be impregnated and spread his

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.940
unholy soul throughout the cosmos.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:20.960
While Raven's mother, Arella,
had originally been fooled by a mystical disguise,

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:26.160
she eventually learned the truth of her daughter's
parentage: the demon Trigon was Raven's father.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.460
Though some on Azarath wary of Raven, given
her demonic ancestry, she was allowed to grow,

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.770
learn, and master her powers within the sanctity
of its borders.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:39.390
But not even an interdimensional Eden could
shelter Raven for long, nor keep her ignorant

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.160
of her father's thirst for power.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.800
Terrified of what he might unleash upon an
unsuspecting populace, Raven traveled to Earth

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.620
and asked the Justice League for aid.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:52.000
When she was turned away, she had no choice
but to gather a team of heroes on her own:

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.480
the lineup that would become the New Teen
Titans.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.720
In this way, Trigon planted the seed of his
own destruction.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:03.480
Fear of him didn't keep Raven quiet, pliable,
or cowed it empowered her to defy him, regardless

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.480
of the consequences.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:09.510
She refused to further her father's destructive
agenda, refused to accept the Justice League's

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:14.700
cold shoulder, and finally, refused to give
in to the Armageddon that Trigon briefly brought

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:15.520
to the Earth.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:20.500
Trigon might've thought fathering half-demon
children would seal his eventual victory,

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.980
but he didn't count on their human halves
winning out.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:34.760
Raven gained her powers through her demonic
parentage, but it was her ability to love,

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:39.900
find fellowship, and work alongside her friends
that truly mattered in the fight against her father.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.560
With Trigon's level of hellish power to deal
with, it makes sense to ask how the Teen Titans

00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:48.880
finally managed to bring down the terror of
a thousand worlds.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:50.310
Well, it wasn't easy.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:55.040
An initial attempt that combined all of the
Titans' powers, Arella's empathic abilities,

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:59.760
and an interdimensional portal, put him away
for a while, but it didn't destroy him entirely.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:05.260
Trigon, ever patient, bided his time, ruminating
upon the abilities of Raven's new team and

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:09.920
how he might counter them, steadily growing
in power until he was able to break free of his bonds.

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:15.800
In one terrifying campaign of violence, Trigon
laid siege to Azarath, murdered its inhabitants,

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:18.060
and corrupted Raven's soul entirely.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.980
But the souls of Azarath hadn't dissolved
into the ether.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:25.960
Being magically powerful, they dwelt within
the Rings of Azar, holy relics worn by Raven.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:31.320
In a complex plan, the Titans were taken over
by Trigon's evil and murdered Raven, a terrible

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:35.380
act that nevertheless allowed the souls of
Azarath to use her as a channel.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:40.499
Trigon was then blasted with pure Azarathian
light, and his soul was disincorporated and

00:04:40.499 --> 00:04:41.969
his body torn apart.

00:04:41.969 --> 00:04:46.740
With Trigon seemingly vanquished, Raven came
back to life, and the world returned to normal.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:51.640
Good had won … but not without a battle
few of the Titans would ever be able to forget.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.400
Raven is, of course, Trigon's most famous
child.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.319
But the legendary baddie made sure to have
far more than one kid to choose from when

00:04:59.319 --> 00:05:01.159
it came to his nefarious plans.

00:05:01.159 --> 00:05:06.520
Hundreds of Trigon's offspring populate the
DC universe, many of them possibly even ignorant

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:07.520
of their heritage.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:12.440
Raven wasn't so lucky, and neither were the
boys who became known as the Sons of Trigon.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:17.839
Introduced in 2008's Titans #3, there were
originally six members of the group called

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:19.200
the Sons of Trigon.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:23.720
Conceived around the same time Raven was,
they were intended to embody the seven deadly

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:26.900
sins, with Raven as the seventh, representing
pride.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:31.640
Jesse, Jared, and Jacob (envy, wrath, and
lust, respectively) emerged as the leaders

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:36.120
of the heinous septet, and they used Raven
as a portal to where their weakened father

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:36.760
slumbered.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:39.540
And yet, they didn't raise him, as you might
expect.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:44.310
Instead, they stole away his power for themselves,
an act so evil that it actually made their

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.009
fearsome father smile.

00:05:46.009 --> 00:05:50.420
They were, of course, eventually defeated
by Raven and the Titans, but the idea of Raven

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:56.240
having siblings was an intriguing enough notion
that after the New 52 reboot, it was reintroduced

00:05:56.249 --> 00:05:59.740
in 2013 in the pages of The Phantom Stranger
#2.

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:04.300
Nowadays, Raven has three brothers named Belial,
Ruskoff, and Suge.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.370
What havoc they might wreak remains to be
seen, but it's a pretty safe bt for readers

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.840
to assume it will be terrible when it arrives.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:16.880
Initially, the New 52 meant a fresh start
for Raven as a typical girl named Rachel Roth.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:20.860
But Trigon's daughter never gets a reprieve
for long, and the Phantom Stranger ultimately

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.260
delivered her back into the arms of her father.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:27.520
After a stretch of time in the "under-realms,"
Raven reemerged as her father's "black bird

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.180
of terror," keen to conquer the world on his
behalf.

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:34.440
Trigon had, in fact, discovered a certain
respect for his daughter over the course of

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:39.100
their time together, naming her as his favorite
child and seeking to use her as a spearhead

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.560
for future attacks on Earth.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:45.659
Naturally, Raven turned against him, saved
the world alongside the Titans, and sent Trigon

00:06:45.659 --> 00:06:47.060
back to where he came from.

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:49.309
She hadn't ever truly been his creature.

00:06:49.309 --> 00:06:51.920
Instead, she'd merely become an impeccable
actress.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:56.340
Even with that, though, Trigon's favoritism
was striking during this period, and he even

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:58.820
desired to install Raven upon the throne.

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:03.360
As Trigon detailed while torturing his other
three children, Raven's knowledge of love,

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:08.599
compassion, and justice would, he believed,
make her a conqueror he himself couldn't become.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:13.580
It's a twisted sort of respect, to be certain,
and still largely self-serving.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:19.480
But for a time, Trigon saw his daughter as
greater than himself, if only in one crucial aspect.

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:24.960
Trigon is an all-star villain, the sort of
world-shattering powerhouse whose appearances

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:29.580
require entire storylines' worth of buildup,
execution, and resolution.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:33.839
His is an evil that extends beyond his own
stories, however, to the point of creating

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.660
entirely separate bad guys.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:40.740
Psimon, an enormously powerful psychic, is
the most famous example of Trigon's proteges.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:45.180
Once a physicist seeking to blaze new trails
in dimensional exploration, he got quite a

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:48.860
bit more than he bargained for when he accidentally
breached Trigon's realm.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:53.860
Seizing this rare opportunity, Trigon imbued
the hapless scientist with devastating mental

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:58.200
abilities, twisted him towards his own desire
to conquer the Earth, and, presumably, told

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:03.220
him to start spelling his name with a silent
P. Psimon set out to further Trigon's mission,

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:08.119
joined the Fearsome Five, and began a long
and ugly career of brutality, manipulation,

00:08:08.119 --> 00:08:09.119
and violence.

00:08:09.119 --> 00:08:13.960
However, he didn't actually end up doing much
to carry out Trigon's plans, and after a stint

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:17.569
of banishment, he appeared to have been forgotten
by his dark master.

00:08:17.569 --> 00:08:22.259
Unfortunately, that didn't stop Psimon from
using his powers for evil, and if anything,

00:08:22.259 --> 00:08:26.860
he'd been freed to create as much panic and
mayhem as he liked, following no agenda but

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.840
his own desire to inflict cruelty.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:34.120
Psimon stands as a monument to Trigon's malice
and power, a decent member of society left

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:37.660
shattered and rotten by a passing glance from
worlds-shaking evil.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:40.300
What Trigon started, though, the Joker ended.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:44.519
When most of DC's villains were trapped on
another planet, Psimon annoyed the Clown Prince

00:08:44.519 --> 00:08:48.940
of Crime so much that he wound up finding
out why it's a bad idea to keep your brain

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:50.340
inside a glass dome.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:55.860
One of the best things about superhero comics
is their multiple-choice approach to storytelling.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:57.240
So it goes with Trigon.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:02.209
Perhaps his most unique form is that of "Das
Trigon," a villain of the DC Bombshells series.

00:09:02.209 --> 00:09:06.709
Within the Bombshells universe, Trigon was
a German mountain spirit whose liaison with

00:09:06.709 --> 00:09:08.440
a human woman led to Raven.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:13.380
Here, Raven grew up in a small Alpine village,
instructed by her grandfather in the control

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:17.160
of her powers until the Joker's daughter upended
her tranquil life.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:21.740
Eventually, Raven rediscovered her father
working for dark masters, but this wasn't

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.800
the aimless evil of Trigon's past.

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:28.600
In this story, Trigon felt utterly untethered
when Raven's mother died, so he gave up on

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:33.820
goodness to join the dastardly General Faora
… until Faora threatened Raven's life.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:38.500
Trigon fell defending his daughter, who buried
him beneath a tree and wept for the father

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.920
she'd never known as well as she would've
liked.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:44.740
It was a very different Trigon, indeed, and
all the more affecting for it.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:50.660
These days, most kids know the Teen Titans
from Teen Titans Go!, where Robin, Starfire,

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:56.000
Beast Boy, Raven, and Cyborg spend more time
scarfing burritos and getting into wacky scrapes

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:58.720
involving waffles than they do crime-fighting.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:03.470
For as off-the-wall as the cartoon is, however,
it digs deeply into DC's vast and complex

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:08.580
history including, of course, Trigon and all
the terror he's visited upon the Titans.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:12.660
But like so many classic characters who've
made an appearance on Teen Titans Go!, this

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:15.940
cartoon version of Trigon is … rather different.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:21.080
Instead of his usual look — you know, capes,
ragged loincloths, giant demonic antlers — he

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:23.560
wears sweater vests, slacks, and neckties.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:28.820
And sure, yes, he's described as the "master
of the dark, destroyer of dimensions, enslaver

00:10:28.829 --> 00:10:33.209
of civilizations," but, well, he does make
sure to always spend Thanksgiving with his

00:10:33.209 --> 00:10:33.920
daughter.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:37.360
And when Demon Prom rolls around, he nominates
Raven for Prom Queen.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:41.560
And he does spend Father's Day leafing through
treasured photos of his baby girl.

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:46.519
Trigon is a bad guy in Teen Titans Go!, but
that doesn't necessarily mean he's a bad dad.

00:10:46.519 --> 00:10:50.560
He might want to rule the Earth, but he also
wants what's best for his precious daughter,

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:52.700
no matter how embarrassed that might make
her.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:58.340
"I'm so proud. The only thing left to do is kill your friends."

00:10:58.340 --> 00:10:59.960
"Kill us kill us!

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.000
You can totally do it!"

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.350
